  "comment": "**What it does**\nFinds companies where **insiders are putting their own money in** - net\ninsider BUYING over the last ~6 months.\n- **The signal** - net buying of at least 4% of insider-held shares (any\n  positive was ~1000 names after the size cut; 4%+ keeps real conviction).\n  Research: buying is the informative side (selling has many innocent reasons).\n- **Where it works** - small/mid caps ($300M-$10B), where the signal is\n  strongest; banks included on purpose (strongest industry per the research).\n- **Not a falling knife** - RS Rank 45+ so you're not catching collapses\n  insiders are averaging into.\nPre-profit names allowed - conviction is the filter, not polish.\nExpect a broad list (hundreds) - this is a signal scan; the sort does the picking.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- More names? `insider_net_buy_pct` back to 2 and `rs_rank` to 40.\n- Conviction shortlist? `insider_net_buy_pct` >= 10.\n- Larger caps too? Raise the cap ceiling (expect a weaker signal there).\n- Add a health floor? `quick_health_score` >= 4 (drops banks/REITs from the\n  screen though - it only exists for standard stocks).\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `growth_score`**, tiebreak `momentum_score`.\n- **Avoid** `overall_score` - it dilutes the one signal this screen is about.\n- The raw `insider_net_buy_pct` column is also worth a sort: biggest\n  conviction first.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find companies where the insiders are putting their own money in \u2014 net insider\nBUYING (the research says buying is the informative side, and the signal is\nstrongest in smaller companies).\n- **Goal**: follow the smart money. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **The signal**: insiders net buying over the last ~6 months.\n- **Where it works**: small and mid caps, roughly $300M-$10B.\n- **Not a falling knife**: some minimum price strength so I'm not catching\n  collapses insiders are averaging into.\n- **Kinds**: normal stocks, banks, insurance and REITs (the signal is actually\n  strongest in banks). **Risk**: volatile OK. Pre-profit OK.\n- **Results**: ~50-300 names. **Sorting**: growth first, tiebreak momentum.",
